Based on my knowledge, the most recent version of the BMW M5 does not come with a V10 engine. The V10 engine was featured in the E60/E61 generation of the BMW M5, produced from 2004 to 2010. The most recent generation of the BMW M5 (G90) features a V8 engine combined with an electric motor as part of a plug-in hybrid system.

Therefore, I cannot provide an evaluation for a "most recent BMW M5 V10" as this configuration does not exist.